# Elegant Sip — environment variables.
#
# All of these are OPTIONAL. Every feature degrades honestly without them:
# nothing in the UI claims a capability that the missing variable would provide.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in what you have.

# ── Contact form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A JSON form backend that accepts POST { name, email, subject, message }.
# Formspree, Basin, Formspark and similar all work.
# WITHOUT IT: the contact form opens the visitor's mail client with the message
# prefilled, and the success screen says so rather than claiming it was sent.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=

# ── Newsletter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An ESP subscribe endpoint accepting POST { email }.
# WITHOUT IT: signups are stored in localStorage only. Either way the WELCOME10
# code is shown on screen and never promised by email.
VITE_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=

# ── Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider must be exactly `plausible` or `ga4`. Events fire ONLY after the
# visitor accepts the consent banner, and PII is never included in event props.
# WITHOUT IT: only the marketing tags below are used.
VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=
VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=

# ── Marketing tags (src/lib/tags.ts) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Tag Manager and the Meta Pixel load ONLY after the visitor accepts the
# cookie banner. Leave these commented out to use the built-in IDs; set one to
# an empty value to switch that tag off.
# VITE_GTM_ID=GTM-W5MN9LMR
# VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=1702510334659568
